# libretranslate
msgid "**Adapter in front of the sidecar:** The ``gitea-mcp`` sidecar runs as compose service ``giteamcpupstream`` on the role’s own network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers ``initialize`` and ``tools/list`` to any caller because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what authenticates: a client presents the ``mcp_bearer`` credential and is refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token upstream via ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``."
msgstr "**Adaptador delante del sidecar:** El ``gitea-mcp`` sidecar funciona como servicio de compostura ``giteamcpupstream`` en la propia red del papel sólo, así que nada más que el adaptador lo alcanza. Respuestas ``initialize`` y ``tools/list`` a cualquier llamador porque no tiene ninguna credencial propia y espera que cada cliente suministre una señal de Gitea por solicitud, lo que hace que no sea seguro exponer directamente. El adaptador es lo que autentica: un cliente presenta el ``mcp_bearer`` credencial y se niega con 401 de lo contrario, y el adaptador presenta el token Gitea picado a través de ``ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY``."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Adapter in front of the sidecar:** The `gitea-mcp` sidecar runs as compose service `giteamcpupstream` on the role's own network only, so nothing but the adapter reaches it. It answers `initialize` and `tools/list` to any caller because it holds no credential of its own and expects each client to supply a Gitea token per request, which makes it unsafe to expose directly. The adapter is what authenticates: a client presents the `mcp_bearer` credential and is refused with 401 otherwise, and the adapter presents the minted Gitea token upstream via `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY`."
